      {
        "id": 544928263,
        "iid": 4038,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "fix(repo): send topics instead of deprecated tag_list",
        "description": "## Description\n\n`glab repo create --tag <value>` puts the values in `CreateProjectOptions.TagList`, which sends the\n`tag_list` API field. GitLab deprecated `tag_list` in 14.0 in favour of `topics`, and client-go marks\nthe field `Deprecated: Use Topics instead`. Because of that, `project_create.go` is one of the files\nlisted in the staticcheck `SA1019` exclusion in `.golangci.yml`, under the TODO\n\"drop these once the deprecated fields are migrated\".\n\nThis MR:\n\n- Sends the `--tag` values as `Topics` instead of `TagList`.\n- Removes `internal/commands/project/create/project_create` from that `SA1019` exclusion.\n- Changes the `--tag` help from \"The list of tags for the project.\" to \"The list of topics for the\n  project.\", which matches the GitLab UI and avoids confusion with Git tags. Docs regenerated with\n  `make gen-docs`.\n- Adds `Test_projectCreateCmd_TagsSentAsTopics`, which checks that `--tag go --tag cli` reaches the\n  API call as `Topics: [\"go\", \"cli\"]`.\n\nThere is no change for users: in GitLab, `Projects::CreateService#build_topics` uses\n`params[:topics] || params[:tag_list]`, so both fields end up in the same place. `topics` has been\naccepted since GitLab 14.0.\n\nThe flag name `--tag` / `-t` stays the same.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nNone found. Searched issues and MRs (all states) for \"TagList\", \"tag_list\", \"topics\",\n\"project topics\", \"repo create tag\", \"SA1019\", \"deprecated fields\".\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- `go run ./cmd/gen-docs/docs.go` (same as `make gen-docs`): only the `--tag` line in\n  `docs/source/repo/create.md` changed.\n- `go build ./...`\n- `go vet ./internal/commands/project/create/`\n- `go test ./internal/commands/project/create/` (all tests pass, including the new one).\n- `staticcheck ./internal/commands/project/create/` reports nothing now, so the exclusion is no\n  longer needed for this file.\n\nThis contribution was prepared with the help of an AI assistant. I reviewed the changes and take responsibility for them.",
